{:tier :glm-5.2, :verse 13, :comments ["<b>Give us meat.</b> They asked improperly, for the manna would transform for them into whatever taste they desired, as it is said: ״ויתן להם שאלתם״. As for meat of cattle and beasts — they already had it, as it is said: ״וגם ערב רב עלה אתם וצאן ובקר״. And if you ask: did they not eat them in the wilderness? Behold it is said: ״ומקנה רב״ etc. From here said Rabbi Shmuel: they craved only forbidden sexual relations, as it is said: ״וימטר עליהם כעפר שאר״ — and 'she'er' means nothing but forbidden sexual relations, as it is said: ״איש אל כל שאר בשרו״. Thus they sought to permit forbidden sexual relations, and likewise it says: ״בוכה למשפחותיו״ — on account of family matters. Therefore it says: ״ויחר אף ה' מאד ובעיני משה רע״. At that moment Moses said to the Holy One, blessed be He: In the past I had with me someone to share the burden of carrying them, for there were seventy elders who were appointed from Mount Sinai, as it is said: ״ויעל משה ואהרן נדב ואביהוא ושבעים מזקני ישראל״. And now I am alone, as it is said: ״לא אוכל לבדי לשאת״. And where were those seventy elders? They died in the מתאוננים, as it is said: ״והאספסף אשר בקרבו״. Rabbi Shimon ben Abba and Rabbi Shimon ben Menasya disagree: one says: this 'asafsuf' is the ערב רב. And one says: these are the seventy elders, for it is said of them: ״אספה לי שבעים איש מזקני ישראל״, and it is written there: ״ותבער בם אש ה' ותאכל בקצה המחנה״. And we expound: 'בקצינים שבמחנה' — the officers of the camp, these are the Sanhedrin. And they were worthy of being burned together with Nadab and Abihu from the time of the giving of the Torah, as it is said: ״ויחזו את האלהים״, and it is said: ״ואל אצילי בני ישראל לא שלח ידו״ etc., and as Targum renders: ״ואל רברבי בני ישראל לא הוה נזקא״ — by inference, they were worthy of harm, of the sending forth of a hand, but the Holy One, blessed be He, did not wish to disrupt the joy of the Torah. He waited for Nadab and Abihu until the eighth day of the inauguration, as Rashi explained above, and for the elders — until here. And likewise it is written in Psalms: ״ותבער אש בעדתם״, and 'עדה' means nothing but Sanhedrin, as it is said: ״ואם מעיני העדה״."], :book :numbers, :voice :daat-zkenim, :lang :en, :chapter 11, :notes {}, :source-witnesses [{"versionTitle" "Sefaria community Hebrew (PD)", "language" "he"}], :timestamp "2026-07-30T13:09:17.234606579Z", :translated-from :he, :model "glm-5.2"}